      "our_prose": "As a cold-hardy herbaceous perennial, potted bee balm overwinters, but container roots are less insulated than in-ground crowns. After the tops die back, cut it down and protect the pot in cold zones (sink it, cluster and mulch, or move to an unheated shelter); it resumes growth from the crown in spring. Divide every 2 to 3 years to keep it vigorous.",
